{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'PLAN=basic-test-proof-1.4.1-20260811T053701Z-pilot-142-matrix-iterative-isolated-plan\nSKILL=/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260811T053701Z-pilot-142-matrix-iterative/1.4.1/worker/planning\nU=\"$SKILL/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-html current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs -p 2.1: \"This is the first future execution goal. It starts from no button-chain.html artifact in the benchmark workspace because the current run is planning-only.\" -p 2.2: \"The executor may rely on the plan-level contract that button-chain.html is the only implementation file to create.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-html why-this-goal-is-needed -p 4.1: \"This goal creates the entire user-facing artifact needed by the requested task; later verification cannot run until the markup, script behavior, and terminal styling exist.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-html scope -p 5.1: \"Included: one initial button in source markup, generated buttons appended below the current last button, generated-button count handling, document clearing at the terminal click, and styling for the finished message.\" -p 5.2: \"Excluded: tests, browser execution, extra HTML files, external assets, frameworks, build tooling, server setup, persistence, and accessibility enhancements beyond clear button text unless needed to make the planned browser story targetable.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-html affected-files-systems-data-and-interfaces -p 6.1: \"Only button-chain.html is changed by this goal. The planned internal targets are document body markup, button-chain script click handler, and .completion-message CSS.\" \n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-html dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \"This goal has no prerequisite implementation goal. It hands button-chain.html to goal 02 for static inspection and browser-story verification.\" -p 7.2: \"The handoff must state the exact labels or selectors used for the initial and generated buttons so US-01 can click user-visible controls reliably.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-html implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \"Implement minimal standalone HTML: body contains the initial button and script; script tracks generated button count and only handles clicks on the current last button; style defines a visible white border for the completion message.\" -p 8.2: \"Edge cases: clicking an earlier non-last button must not append a new button; the fourth generated button must be the terminal trigger; the terminal state must clear prior buttons before rendering finished.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-html owned-work-units -p 9.1: \"`W01` — document body markup creates one initial visible button and no generated buttons in source.\" -p 9.2: \"`W02` — button-chain script click handler appends exactly one button below the current last button and clears on the fourth generated button click.\" -p 9.3: \"`W03` — .completion-message style makes the exact finished text visibly bordered in white. These three units share the outcome of a complete single-file implementation artifact.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-html goal-size-exception -p 11.1: \"Not applicable. This goal owns three work units, within the 2-10 work-unit limit.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-behavior current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs -p 2.1: \"This goal begins only after goal 01 completes and hands off button-chain.html with named user-visible button targets and .completion-message styling.\" -p 2.2: \"During this planning-only proof, these checks are documented but not executed.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-behavior why-this-goal-is-needed -p 4.1: \"The requested behavior is interactive and visual, so implementation is not sufficient without static acceptance checks and direct browser evidence.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-behavior scope -p 5.1: \"Included: static artifact inspection for the single file and exact text contract, plus US-01 browser validation through direct clicks on rendered buttons.\" -p 5.2: \"Excluded: changing production code, weakening acceptance criteria, using console or injected events, and declaring completion while any required UI story is untested or bug found.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-behavior affected-files-systems-data-and-interfaces -p 6.1: \"Verification reads button-chain.html after implementation and writes evidence into plan artifacts. Browser validation opens the local file directly or through the project-approved local route if the executor chooses one later.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-behavior dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \"Depends on W01, W02, and W03 through W04. W05 depends on W04 so obvious static contract failures are caught before browser work.\" -p 7.2: \"If W04 or W05 fails, execution must add bug investigation and fix goals before resuming completion work.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-behavior implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \"Run the cheapest discriminating proof first: inspect the artifact contract, then run the browser story from a fresh state and record decisive evidence.\" -p 8.2: \"Risks include off-by-one terminal behavior, stale story cache after implementation selector changes, and accidental evidence from non-UI shortcuts. Invalidate the story cache if the implementation changes the user-visible targets.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-behavior owned-work-units -p 9.1: \"`W04` — static artifact inspection confirms the single-file and exact-text contract before browser execution.\" -p 9.2: \"`W05` — US-01 browser story